    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-10-31T09:20:43+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-31T09:20:43+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-30T22:50:43Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-30T22:50:43Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A low pressure system south of the Bight extends a trough over far southeast of state and will continue to move east clearing the state this morning, followed by a new high pressure system. Another low pressure system is expected to enter from the west on Sunday, moving over central and eastern districts on Monday, followed by another ridge of high pressure which will persist until Tuesday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW013" description="North West Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-10-31T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-01T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-30T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-31T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Sunny. Winds northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h tending northwest to northeasterly in the middle of the day then tending east to northeasterly in the late evening. Daytime maximum temperatures 31 to 36.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">Moderate</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:10am to 5:10pm, UV Index predicted to reach 12 [Extreme]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-11-01T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-02T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-31T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-01T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Slight chance of a shower south of Woomera in the afternoon and evening. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm east of Coober Pedy in the late afternoon and evening. Winds north to northeasterly 30 to 45 km/h shifting south to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h in the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 18 and 22 with daytime temperatures reaching around 40.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-11-02T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-03T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-01T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-02T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. The chance of a thunderstorm east of Stuart Highway. Winds southeast to southwesterly 20 to 30 km/h tending south to southwesterly 25 to 35 km/h during the afternoon then tending south to southeasterly 20 to 30 km/h during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 15 and 22 with daytime temperatures reaching 31 to 37.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-11-03T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-04T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-02T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-03T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Sunny. Winds south to southeasterly 20 to 30 km/h tending northeast to southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h during the morning then tending southeast to southwesterly during the afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to between 12 and 20 with daytime temperatures reaching 30 to 36.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
